BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Breadwinner
DTSTART:20260528T220000Z
DTEND:20260529T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260528T220000Z
UID:189505
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nStarring record-shattering comedi
 an Nate Bargatze in his first feature film\, The Breadwinner stars \nBarga
 tze as salesman Nate Wilcox and Mandy Moore as his wife\, Katie. To Nate a
 nd their three children\, Katie is the \nultimate mom - she manages their 
 comically chaotic household with equal parts efficiency and love\, and eve
 rything \nruns perfectly. But when Katie’s household invention leads to 
 a once-in-a-lifetime deal on Shark Tank and takes her on \na prolonged bus
 iness trip\, Nate has to figure out how to keep the house from (literally)
  falling apart. He and his kids \nsoon learn that while he may not do it l
 ike mom\, he can figure out how to do it his way. Welcome to the dad era.\
 n\nDirected by Eric Appel\n\nScreen 2\n\nEstimated start: 22:25
LOCATION:Regal Bella Bottega\, 8890 NE 161st Avenue\, Redmond\, WA 98052
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Project Hail Mary
DTSTART:20260528T122000Z
DTEND:20260528T152500Z
DTSTAMP:20260528T122000Z
UID:193582
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 156 mins (2h36m)\n\nScience teacher Ryland Grace (Ry
 an Gosling) wakes up on a spaceship light years from home with no recollec
 tion of who he is or how he got there. As his memory returns\, he begins t
 o uncover his mission: solve the riddle of the mysterious substance causin
 g the sun to die out. He must call on his scientific knowledge and unortho
 dox ideas to save everything on Earth from extinction… but an unexpected
  friendship means he may not have to do it alone.\n\nDirected by Christoph
 er Miller & Phil Lord\n\nScreen 6\n\nEstimated start: 12:45
LOCATION:Regal Bella Bottega\, 8890 NE 161st Avenue\, Redmond\, WA 98052
END:VEVENT
