SUMMARY:Scary Movie (Open Cap/Eng Sub)
DTSTART:20260609T211000Z
DTEND:20260609T231500Z
DTSTAMP:20260609T211000Z
UID:193327
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nTwenty-six years after outrunning
  a suspiciously familiar masked killer (“Ghostface”)\, the Core Four a
 re back in the killer’s crosshairs and no horror movie IP is safe. Marlo
 n Wayans (“Shorty”)\, Shawn Wayans (“Ray”)\, Anna Faris (“Cindy
 ”)\, and Regina Hall (“Brenda”) reunite in Scary Movie alongside ret
 urning favorites and fresh faces to slash through reboots\, remakes\, requ
 els\, prequels\, sequels\, spin-offs\, elevated horror\, origin stories\, 
 anything with the word legacy in it\, and every “final chapter” that a
 bsolutely isn’t final. Nothing is sacred. No trope survives. Every line 
 gets crossed.  The Wayans are back to cancel the Cancel Culture.\n\nDirect
 ed by \n\nScreen 6\n\nEstimated start: 21:35
LOCATION:Regal Bella Bottega\, 8890 NE 161st Avenue\, Redmond\, WA 98052
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:David
DTSTART:20260610T110000Z
DTEND:20260610T131500Z
DTSTAMP:20260610T110000Z
UID:192570
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nFrom the songs of his mother’s
  heart to the whispers of a faithful God\, David’s story begins in quiet
  devotion. When the giant Goliath rises to terrorize a nation\, a young sh
 epherd armed with only a sling\, a few stones\, and unshakable faith steps
  forward. Pursued by power and driven by purpose\, his journey tests the l
 imits of loyalty\, love\, and courage—culminating in a battle not just f
 or a crown\, but for the soul of a kingdom.\n\nDirected by Brent Dawes & P
 hil Cunningham\n\nScreen 7\n\nEstimated start: 11:25
LOCATION:Regal Bella Bottega\, 8890 NE 161st Avenue\, Redmond\, WA 98052
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kung Fu Panda 4
DTSTART:20260610T110000Z
DTEND:20260610T130000Z
DTSTAMP:20260610T110000Z
UID:192571
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 94 mins (1h34m)\n\nAfter three death-defying adventu
 res defeating world-class villains with his unmatched courage and mad mart
 ial arts skills\, Po\, the Dragon Warrior (Golden Globe nominee Jack Black
 )\, is called upon by destiny to … give it a rest already. More specific
 ally\, he’s tapped to become the Spiritual Leader of the Valley of Peace
 .\n\nThat poses a couple of obvious problems. First\, Po knows as much abo
 ut spiritual leadership as he does about the paleo diet\, and second\, he 
 needs to quickly find and train a new Dragon Warrior before he can assume 
 his new lofty position.\n\nEven worse\, there’s been a recent sighting o
 f a wicked\, powerful sorceress\, Chameleon (Oscar® winner Viola Davis)\,
  a tiny lizard who can shapeshift into any creature\, large or small. And 
 Chameleon has her greedy\, beady little eyes on Po’s Staff of Wisdom\, w
 hich would give her the power to re-summon all the master villains whom Po
  has vanquished to the spirit realm.\n\nSo\, Po’s going to need some hel
 p. He finds it (kinda?) in the form of crafty\, quick-witted thief Zhen (G
 olden Globe winner Awkwafina)\, a corsac fox who really gets under Po’s 
 fur but whose skills will prove invaluable. In their quest to protect the 
 Valley of Peace from Chameleon’s reptilian claws\, this comedic odd-coup
 le duo will have to work together. In the process\, Po will discover that 
 heroes can be found in the most unexpected places.\n\nDirected by Mike Mit
 chell\n\nScreen 4\n\nEstimated start: 11:25
LOCATION:Regal Bella Bottega\, 8890 NE 161st Avenue\, Redmond\, WA 98052
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Masters of the Universe (Open Cap/Eng Sub)
