BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Citizen Kane
DTSTART:20260705T160000Z
DTEND:20260705T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260705T160000Z
UID:188102
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 124 mins (2h04m)\n\n1940. Alone at his fantastic est
 ate known as Xanadu\, 70-year-old Charles Foster Kane dies\, uttering only
  the single word Rosebud.\n\nSo ends the odyssey of a life ... and begins 
 a fabulous tale of the rise to wealth and power--and ultimate fall--of a c
 omplex man: A boy abandoned by his parents inherits a fortune\, builds a g
 lobal newspaper empire and aspires to become President of the United State
 s\, but he loses everything over an affair with an untalented nightclub si
 nger. This fascinating story unfolds through the eyes of the people import
 ant to the tycoon--each showing a different aspect of Citizen Kane.\n\nThi
 s special 85th anniversary release includes exclusive insight from Leonard
  Maltin.\n\nFathom events do not qualify for Unlimited subscriptions.\n\nD
 irected by Orson Welles\n\nScreen 11\n\nEstimated start: 16:25
LOCATION:Regal Bella Bottega\, 8890 NE 161st Avenue\, Redmond\, WA 98052
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonic the Hedgehog 3
DTSTART:20260706T110000Z
DTEND:20260706T131500Z
DTSTAMP:20260706T110000Z
UID:192598
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nSonic the Hedgehog returns to th
 e big screen this holiday season in his most thrilling adventure yet. Soni
 c\, Knuckles\, and Tails reunite against a powerful new adversary\, Shadow
 \, a mysterious villain with powers unlike anything they have faced before
 . With their abilities outmatched in every way\, Team Sonic must seek out 
 an unlikely alliance in hopes of stopping Shadow and protecting the planet
 .\n\n \n\nDirector Jeff Fowler returns along with our all-star cast includ
 ing Jim Carrey\, Ben Schwartz\, James Marsden\, Tika Sumpter\, Idris Elba\
 , Colleen O’Shaughnessey\, Natasha Rothwell\, Shemar Moore\, Adam Pally\
 , Lee Majdoub\, newcomers Alyla Browne and Krysten Ritter\, with Keanu Ree
 ves joining the franchise as Shadow the Hedgehog.\n\nDirected by Jeff Fowl
 er\n\nScreen 4\n\nEstimated start: 11:25
LOCATION:Regal Bella Bottega\, 8890 NE 161st Avenue\, Redmond\, WA 98052
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Train Your Dragon
DTSTART:20260706T110000Z
DTEND:20260706T133000Z
DTSTAMP:20260706T110000Z
UID:192599
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 125 mins (2h05m)\n\nFrom three-time Oscar® nominee 
 and Golden Globe winner Dean DeBlois\, the creative visionary behind Dream
 Works Animation’s acclaimed How to Train Your Dragon trilogy\, comes a s
 tunning live-action reimagining of the film that launched the beloved fran
 chise.  \n\nOn the rugged isle of Berk\, where Vikings and dragons have be
 en bitter enemies for generations\, Hiccup (Mason Thames\; The Black Phone
 \, For All Mankind) stands apart. The inventive yet overlooked son of Chie
 f Stoick the Vast (Gerard Butler\, reprising his voice role from the anima
 ted franchise)\, Hiccup defies centuries of tradition when he befriends To
 othless\, a feared Night Fury dragon. Their unlikely bond reveals the true
  nature of dragons\, challenging the very foundations of Viking society.  
 \n\nWith the fierce and ambitious Astrid (BAFTA nominee Nico Parker\; Dumb
 o\, The Last of Us) and the village’s quirky blacksmith Gobber (Nick Fro
 st\; Snow White and the Huntsman\, Shaun of the Dead) by his side\, Hiccup
  confronts a world torn by fear and misunderstanding.  \n\nAs an ancient t
 hreat emerges\, endangering both Vikings and dragons\, Hiccup’s friendsh
 ip with Toothless becomes the key to forging a new future. Together\, they
  must navigate the delicate path toward peace\, soaring beyond the boundar
 ies of their worlds and redefining what it means to be a hero and a leader
 . \n\nThe film also stars Julian Dennison (Deadpool 2)\, Gabriel Howell (B
 odies)\, Bronwyn James (Wicked)\, Harry Trevaldwyn (Smothered)\, Ruth Codd
  (The Midnight Club)\, BAFTA nominee Peter Serafinowicz (Guardians of the 
 Galaxy) and Murray McArthur (Game of Thrones).\n\nDirected by Dean DeBlois
 \n\nScreen 2\n\nEstimated start: 11:25
LOCATION:Regal Bella Bottega\, 8890 NE 161st Avenue\, Redmond\, WA 98052
END:VEVENT
